  "correction_rules": [
    "Model tends to overestimate prices in the short term (1-3 days) after recent spikes, especially when sentiment is neutral or slightly positive.",
    "Mean reversion is strong in the 7-14 day horizon; forecasts should be adjusted downward if prices exceed 1.5x the 30-day moving average.",
    "Overshoots after spikes (e.g., +10%+ above peak) are common; apply a 10-20% dampening factor to forecasts in the 3-7 day window post-spike.",
    "Sentiment = 0.00 implies no directional bias; forecasts should be anchored to recent 18-day average, not extrapolated.",
    "Long-term (15+ day) forecasts show persistent downward bias; adjust downward by 5-10% if true outcome is below 70% of 30-day forecast mean.",
    "If true outcome drops below 65% of 30-day forecast mean, apply a corrective lag: subtract 0.5x the previous day’s forecast error."
  ]
